# =====================================================================
# Release V110 -- Patients-by-Plan: Standard_Payment_Plan on Dim_Patients
# =====================================================================
# Denormalises the standardised payment-plan name onto Gold.Dim_Patients so patients slice by plan
# with no model relationship (Payment_Plan_ID is per-tenant -> a natural-key relationship fans out
# across tenants). MIGRATE adds the column in place (existing rows preserved); DEPLOY updates the
# load to derive it (dedup Silver.Payment_Plans + Input.Payment_Plan_Map override) and includes it in
# the change hash so the reload UPDATEs every existing patient. MIGRATE must precede DEPLOY (Fabric
# validates columns at CREATE time). Gold.Dim_Patients.Table.sql is updated in the repo for fresh
# builds but NOT deployed here (DROP/CREATE would wipe the 170k-row table).
#
# APPLY: after deploy, reload Dim_Patients (Orchestrate_Build, or EXEC Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Patients),
# which also regenerates the PBI views (List Patients gains "Standard Payment Plan"); then refresh
# the model. The My Data "Patients by Plan" donut binds to List Patients[Standard Payment Plan].
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V110__patient_standard_payment_plan.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

MIGRATE  Migrations\V110__patient_standard_payment_plan.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Patients.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
